{
  "comment": "What scripts/third-party-notices.py cannot read from the build tree. 'swift' says, for every package of Package.resolved, whether it is linked into the app ('probe' is a symbol prefix that nm finds in the engine when it is). 'extra' lists code that lives inside another package without metadata of its own; 'with' records the version of the host package it was checked against. 'binaries' claims the native libraries of the sidecar that no package record explains. Paths in 'files' start at the repository root.",

  "sections": {
    "swift": "Linked into the app's audio engine.",
    "python": "Installed in the Python environment that runs the Intermediate and Pro levels of Studio (`Contents/Resources/sidecar`). They ship with their source files.",
    "packages": "Code that the Python packages above carry inside them: compiled into their modules, copied next to them, or ported from another project.",
    "runtime": "The Python interpreter in `Contents/Resources/sidecar/python` is a python-build-standalone distribution. These are the libraries linked into it; zlib, libedit and ncurses come from macOS and are not part of the app."
  },

